@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Partner Integration
	Testing user partner updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner2                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner2                          |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner3                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner3                          |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Member" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Watcher" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page	

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View new partner workers
	New partner workers who are added to Zendesk via OSB sync should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_partner" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_partner" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_partner" tag

Scenario: View resynced partner workers
	Partner workers who are resynced to Zendesk should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I remove a user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I remove a user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I remove a user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken"
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I sync the project with the code "ZENOSBA" to zendesk
	Then the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_partner" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should have the "osb_partner" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_partner" tag

