Scenario: View expired project partner worker updates
	If a project's order becomes inactive in OSB, existing partner workers on that project should have their tags removed and also be removed from their organization in Zendesk.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Portal Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	Then the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_partner" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_partner" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should not have the "osb_partner" tag

Scenario: View partner manager removal updates
	If a manager is removed from a partner tied to a project in OSB, the manager's tags should be removed and the manager should also be removed from the organization in Zendesk.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
